{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions order-of-accuracy driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/godunov_norm_D1_periodic on the periodic unit interval [0,1]. Forced-steady eikonal / Hamilton-Jacobi equation u_t = -S|u_x| + S|g'(x)| with the manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x): because u_t = -S|g'| + S|g'| = 0, g is the EXACT solution of the continuous forced PDE for all t (both the initial condition and the steady state), so the analytic reference at every time is g itself. The forcing S|g'(x)| = 2 pi S |cos(2 pi x)| is the constant-in-time source that balances the operator. Discretely u_t = S*(|g'| - godunov(u)); starting from u(0) = g the imbalance is exactly the first-order truncation error S*(|g'| - godunov(g)) = O(dx), so the discrete solution drifts from g at rate O(dx) and the L2 / Linf error at the assert time falls as O(dx) — expected order 1. THE KINKS ARE NOT A PROBLEM: |g'| = 2 pi |cos(2 pi x)| has slope-sign kinks at x = 1/4, 3/4 (where u_x changes sign), yet the Godunov / Rouy-Tourin entropy fix sqrt(max(D-,0)^2 + min(D+,0)^2) selects the correct one-sided branch through the kink, so the scheme retains clean first-order accuracy in L2 AND Linf uniformly (numerically verified: pairwise orders 0.98 -> 1.00 across N = 16..256, Linf likewise). This is the property that distinguishes the Godunov norm from a naive centered |u_x| and the reason a periodic sin MMS — whose |g'| necessarily changes sign — still converges at order 1. Both g and |g'| are periodic (g(0) = g(1) = 0, |cos| has period 1/2), so the periodic wrap is fully consistent (no seam artifact), unlike a non-periodic ramp; the two wrap faces converge at the same order-1 rate as the interior, so the state L2/Linf reduction over the whole field is a clean order-1 gate with nothing to exempt. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing the extent by the metaparameter name N, esm-spec 9.7.6, so the loader-API rebinding of N for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent). The ic, the forcing observed, and the test reference spell the cell-center coordinate x_i = (i - 1/2)/N inline from literals and the metaparameter N (the 6.6.5/ic build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free; build-time coordinate expressions fold from literals and N alone, never the free-name x_coord template). Per-resolution error norms are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis, 29(3), 867-884. Convergence of the monotone Godunov Hamiltonian sqrt(max(D-,0)^2 + min(D+,0)^2) to the viscosity solution of the eikonal equation at first order.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Osher, S., & Sethian, J. A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed: Algorithms based on Hamilton-Jacobi formulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 79(1), 12-49. The upwind entropy construction of |grad phi| for level-set Hamilton-Jacobi terms.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GodunovEikonalMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/godunov_norm_D1_periodic.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Level-set field integrated under the forced eikonal u_t = -S*godunov(u) + S|g'|; starts at and stays near the manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x), deviating by the O(dx) truncation error."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi speed (u_t = -S|u_x|). The forcing carries the matching S so g is the exact steady solution for any S > 0."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "forcing": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "The manufactured source S|g'(x)| = 2 pi S |cos(2 pi x_i)|, a spatially varying constant-in-time field (S folded via the du/dt scaling; here the |g'| factor, x_i = (i - 1/2)/N spelled inline). It exactly balances the continuous operator so g = sin(2 pi x) is the steady exact solution; the residual after discretization is the O(dx) truncation error."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "sin",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  6.283185307179586,
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "i",
                            0.5
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "/",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            "N"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "S",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "forcing",
                  {
                    "op": "sqrt",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "^",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "D",
                            "args": [
                              "u"
                            ],
                            "wrt": "x"
                          },
                          2
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "forcing",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                6.283185307179586,
                {
                  "op": "abs",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "cos",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            6.283185307179586,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_eikonal",
          "description": "Manufactured solution g(x) = sin(2 pi x), S = 1. Derivation: u_t = -S|u_x| + S|g'| with u(0) = g gives u_t = 0 at the continuous level, so g is the exact solution for all t; discretely u_t = S*(|g'| - godunov(u)) and the initial imbalance is the truncation error S*(|g'| - godunov(g)) = O(dx), so u drifts from g at O(dx) and ||u(T) - g|| = O(dx). References evaluate g at the cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (L2_error 0 within 1e-9). The t=0.2 assertion bounds the first-order error (about 4% relative L2 at N=64, comfortably under the 0.1 cap, which holds across the sweep). Exact per-resolution L2/Linf errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_mms/golden/errors.json; the observed order is asserted to be 1.0 +/- 0.15 by scripts/check_convergence_order.py.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.2
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.2,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.1
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
